.TH ZERODDS-RECORD 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-record \- capture and inspect ZeroDDS .zddsrec files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-record record
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR]...
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
[\fB\-\-max\-sample\-bytes\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-decode\fR \fB\-\-type\-file\fR \fIIDL\fR]
[\fB\-\-map\fR \fITOPIC=Type\fR]...
[\fB\-\-out\-json\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-out\-sqlite\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-dialect\fR \fINAME\fR]
.PP
.B zerodds-record info
.I FILE
.PP
.B zerodds-record list
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-record
captures live DDS topics into a versioned binary
.B .zddsrec
file and reads existing files for inspection.
.PP
The
.B record
sub-command starts a DCPS runtime, registers a user-reader per
.B \-\-topic
flag, and writes every received sample into the output file. Recording
stops on
.B SIGINT
or after
.B \-\-duration
elapses.
.PP
.B info
parses the file header and prints time-base, participants and topic
list.
.B list
counts frames per topic.
.SH OPTIONS FOR record
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output path. Default: \fIcapture\-<unix-ts>.zddsrec\fR.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic to subscribe (repeatable, at least one required).
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Recording duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR. Default:
indefinite (until SIGINT).
.TP
.BR \-\-max\-sample\-bytes " " \fIN\fR
DoS cap per sample. Default: 1048576.
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
The base configuration file; its sibling
.IR PATH .d/
holds drop-ins. Default: the system configuration directory
.RI ( /etc/zerodds
on Linux,
.I /usr/local/etc/zerodds
on macOS).
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH DECODED OUTPUT FOR record
The opaque
.B .zddsrec
is always written as well.
.TP
.BR \-\-decode
Decode samples to typed values. Needs
.BR \-\-type\-file .
.TP
.BR \-\-type\-file " " \fIIDL\fR
Out-of-band IDL providing the types.
.TP
.BR \-\-map " " \fITOPIC=Type\fR
Override which IDL type decodes a topic (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-out\-json " " \fIFILE\fR
Write decoded samples as NDJSON.
.TP
.BR \-\-out\-sqlite " " \fIFILE\fR
Write decoded samples to per-topic SQLite. An existing FILE is replaced, as
with \fB\-o\fR and \fB\-\-out\-json\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-dialect " " \fINAME\fR
The wire dialect to decode in: \fIcyclone\fR, \fIrti\fR, \fIfastdds\fR,
\fIopendds\fR and the others \fBzerodds\-idlc generate \-\-dialect\fR takes.
Default: the configuration's \fBwire.codec_dialect\fR, itself \fIspecification\fR
unless set. The decoder does not infer it from the bytes;
a sample written in another dialect is reported, not accepted.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I capture-<unix-ts>.zddsrec
Default output filename when
.B \-\-output
is not given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-admin (1),
.BR zerodds-replay (1)
.PP
